  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Agro Business Trade</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This trade mission aims to stimulate business-to-business cooperation and knowledge exchange between the Netherlands and Pakistan in onion, potato and vegetable (tomatoes and carrots) and dairy chains and to assist in improving the enabling environment for agribusiness. The mission will last four days in November 2018 and include meetings with officials, farmers, and businesses. There will be opportunities for Dutch and local companies to connect, exchange knowledge, and participate in individual matchmaking sessions. The current challenges in Pakistani agriculture include limited water and low water efficiency, lacking food safety due to lack of enforcement of regulations, lack of improved varieties, low productivity, high post-harvest losses, lack of cooling facilities, low-quality animal feed, etcetera. By linking Dutch agricultural firms and training institutes with Pakistani agricultural companies and counterparts and through the exchange of knowledge and the establishment of partnerships, can several of these challenges be tackled.</narrative>
  </description>
